  "cli_result_text": "Submitted the 14 files most relevant to tracing this contract drift, ranked by importance:\n\n**FastAPI request validation chain:**\n1. `fastapi/dependencies/utils.py` \u2014 `solve_dependencies`, `request_body_to_args`: core body parsing/validation logic\n2. `fastapi/routing.py` \u2014 the `app()` request handler that reads `request.body()`, checks Content-Type, and drives dependency resolution\n3. `fastapi/_compat.py` \u2014 Pydantic v1/v2 compatibility shim; where v2 validation semantics (nested models, unions, defaults) actually get invoked\n4. `fastapi/exceptions.py` / `fastapi/exception_handlers.py` \u2014 how validation failures become 422 responses\n5. `fastapi/encoders.py` \u2014 `jsonable_encoder`, relevant for symmetry with how bodies are serialized\n6. `fastapi/params.py` \u2014 `Body`/field param definitions (defaults, embedding behavior)\n7. `fastapi/applications.py` \u2014 top-level app wiring for exception handling\n\n**httpx request encoding chain:**\n1. `httpx/_content.py` \u2014 JSON body encoding (`encode_json`), where `None`/default handling and Content-Type header logic live\n2. `httpx/_models.py` \u2014 `Request`/`Content` construction, header assembly\n3. `httpx/_client.py` \u2014 request-building entry points (`.post()`, `.request()`) that route into content encoding\n4. `httpx/_types.py` \u2014 type definitions for request content/JSON params\n5. `httpx/_api.py` \u2014 top-level convenience functions\n6. `httpx/_multipart.py` \u2014 alternate encoding path, useful for contrast with JSON encoding",
